I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw`, so it has no `http-client` import, and adding one would widen its authority beyond what it was granted. The fetch would also send the digest's date and item ids to an external host on every call. `published-digest` has no free-text field, so the query would be built from those identifiers.

I also assumed that `RecordSeen` marks every considered id as seen whether or not the digest was published, since the `selection` contract says all considered items should be marked.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in published.considered.iter() {
            state_rw::put(id.as_str(), published.date.as_str());
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

